# 04: Remove legacy provider construction

**Blocked by:** 02, 03
**Status:** open

## Delivery

All provider selection flows through application composition and the legacy entry point is absent.

## Design context

The compatibility path defined by the [provider composition seam](../design.md#provider-composition-seam) can close after [CLI migration](02-migrate-cli.example) and [server migration](03-migrate-server.example), while preserving the required [provider behavior](../requirements.md#provider-behavior).

## Touch points

Legacy web construction entry point and repository call sites.

## Changes

1. Remove the legacy entry point and compatibility adapter.
2. Remove remaining legacy references.

## Constraints

Concrete provider construction remains encapsulated by the web adapter.

## Done and verify

Repository search finds no legacy callers and all provider behavior tests pass; run `go test ./internal/...` and `rg "legacy provider constructor" .` expecting no matches.
